WEBVTT

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:02.140
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> <b>Visit Scotland</b>

00:00:02.973 --> 00:00:10.527
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Scotland is one of the world’s top tourist destinations, with 10,000 kilometres of coast,

00:00:10.685 --> 00:00:19.894
790 islands, more than 30,000 ‘lochs’ (the word in Scotland for lakes), famous castles,

00:00:19.895 --> 00:00:21.892
and beautiful cities.

00:00:22.278 --> 00:00:25.332
There’s something for visitors of all ages.

00:00:26.363 --> 00:00:28.036
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> <b>Why Loch Ness?</b>

00:00:28.963 --> 00:00:36.332
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Loch Ness is 10 km south west of the city of Inverness – perfect for day trips.

00:00:36.772 --> 00:00:44.945
You can take a boat trip on the loch and visit the Loch Ness Centre to find out all about ‘Nessie’, the monster.

00:00:45.772 --> 00:00:52.658
One of the most beautiful castles in the world, Urquhart Castle, is on the banks of the loch.

00:00:53.198 --> 00:00:57.616
There are wonderful places for walking and cycling very near.

00:00:58.878 --> 00:01:00.058
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> <b>Accommodation</b>

00:01:00.932 --> 00:01:07.550
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Stay at the Craigdarroch Hotel. It’s the perfect place for a great view of the loch.